      <minor />
      <comment>Please provide references that Roy Desjardins attended [[Conestoga College]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Dorimène Roy Desjardins''' (-[[1932]]) and her husband [[Alphonse Desjardins (co-operator)|Alphonse Desjardins]] were co-founders of the ''Caisses populaires Desjardins'' (today [[Mouvement Desjardins]]), a forerunner of [[North America]]n [[credit union]]s.

Note that her husband was not the same person as a contemporary mayor of Montreal also named [[Alphonse Desjardins (politician)|Alphonse Desjardins]].

[[Category:1932 deaths|Desjardins, Dorimène Roy]]
[[Category:Canadian businesspeople|Desjardins, Dorimène Roy]]
[[Category:People from Quebec|Desjardins, Dorimène Roy]]</text>
    </revision>
