    <title>Aldgate</title>
    <id>246137</id>
    <revision>
      <id>25751201</id>
      <timestamp>2005-10-17T17:00:24Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Dominic Sayers</username>
        <id>443340</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Chaucer factoid</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{otheruses}}
{{infobox CoL|
   |Ward=              Aldgate
   |PostCode=          [[London EC3|EC3]]          
   |GridReference=     TQ334813 
}}
'''Aldgate''' was a gateway through [[London Wall]] from the [[City of London]] to [[Whitechapel]] and the [[East End of London|East End]].

From [[1374]] until [[1386]], [[Geoffrey Chaucer]] occupied a dwelling above the Aldgate.

In [[1773]], ''[[Poems on Various Subjects, Religious and Moral]]'' by [[Phillis Wheatley]], the first book by an [[African American]] was published here after her owners could not find a publisher in [[Boston]].

Aldgate is a [[ward (politics)|ward]] electing councillors to the [[Corporation of London]].

Stations near Aldgate:
* [[Aldgate tube station]]
* [[Aldgate East tube station]]

{{gbmapping|TQ337813}}

==See also==
*[[City gate]]
*[[City wall]]

{{London-geo-stub}}

[[no:Aldgate]]
[[Category:Districts of London]]
[[Category:London Wall and its gates]]
[[Category:City of London]]</text>
