  <page>
    <title>Gavius</title>
    <id>246179</id>
    <revision>
      <id>16123041</id>
      <timestamp>2005-03-14T16:56:11Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>BerndGehrmann</username>
        <id>209196</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>de:</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Gavius''' was the [[nomen]] of the ancient [[Rome|Roman]] '''''gens Gavia'''''.  The [[Gavi Arch]] in [[Verona, Italy|Verona]] was built in honor of the ''gens''.

* [[Gavius Bassus]], writer at time of [[Cicero]]
* Gavius Silo, orator heard by [[Augustus Caesar]] in [[26 BC]], mentioned by [[Seneca the Younger|Seneca]]
* [[Marcus Gavius Apicius]], gourmet [[1st century]] AD
* [[Gavius Silvanus]], tribune of [[Nero]]
* Marcus Gavius [[Claudius]] Squilla Gallicanus, consul [[127]]
* Marcus Gavius Squilla Gallicanus, consul [[151]]
* Marcus Gavius Orfitus, consul [[165]]
* Marcus Gavius Cornelius Cethegus, consul [[170]]
* Lucius [[Fulvius]] Gavius Numisius [[Petronius]] Aemilianus, [[206]]

[[Gavius Pontius]] was a [[Samnite]] general ca. [[321 BC]].

[[Category:Families of Rome]]
[[de:Gavier]]</text>
